<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bangka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Banka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bangka is an island off the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, part of the province of Bangka <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belitung">Belitung</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">Tin</a> was found there around 1710, and under the Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule it became one of the world's main tin producers, worked largely by Chinese miners. The Dutch took direct control in the early 19th century.</p></div>
